INT. ORBITAL STATION "HALCYON" - OBSERVATION RING - SHIP NIGHT

A curved window onto a gray world. Four crew in thermal suits sit at a low table around a flickering screen.

COMMANDER YUSUF ADEWUNMI-LINDGREN (50s) speaks first. DR. HELENA OKONKWO-BRANDT (40s) answers. ENGINEER TOMASZ NAKASHIMA-AMADI (30s) interrupts. And the youngest, TECH IRIS MBEKI-HALVORSEN (20s), says nothing.

YUSUF
Final report. Oxygen reserves at eleven percent.

HELENA
That's four days.

TOMASZ
Four days if nobody breathes.

YUSUF
Nobody's counting breaths, Tomasz.

TOMASZ
I am.

HELENA
Commander, the relief ship?

YUSUF
Nine days out.

HELENA
Then we're five short.

TOMASZ
Five.

YUSUF
We are going to be fine.

IRIS
(quietly)
No, we're not.

They look at her. She looks at the window.

IRIS (CONT'D)
But we can say it like we are.

Yusuf nods. Helena reaches across the table and takes Iris's hand. Tomasz folds his arms and stares at the gray world turning below.
